#!/usr/bin/env python3
# run_block-repo: vitalio/run_block
"""Usage:
  {prog} <session>/<step>            Run a Bash block from stdin
  {prog} --fix <session>/<target>    Patch <target>.sh via Python on stdin and run as <target>_N
  {prog} --retry [session/step]      Re-run the last block (or a specific block, e.g. after aborting)
  {prog} --list | -l [session]       List sessions or steps in a session with their status
  {prog} --show [session/step]       Show saved script and output of the last (or specified) block
  {prog} --start [--force] [session] Create a new session directory in {base_dir}/ (default: s1, s2, ...)
  {prog} --agents-install [FILE]      Install or update {prog} instructions in FILE (default: {agents_file})
  {prog} --agents                    Print Markdown instructions for AI agents (for AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md)
  {prog} --config                    Show active configuration and config file path
  {prog} --init-config [--force]     Create a commented default config file at {config_path}
  {prog} --update [--force]          Self-update {prog} from GitHub (vitalio/run_block)
  {prog} --check-update              Check if a newer version is available on GitHub
  {prog} -V | --version              Print version and exit 0
  {prog} -h | --help                 Print this usage and exit 0

Reads a Bash script (or Python patch in --fix mode) from stdin, saves it under
{base_dir}/<session>/, checks syntax with bash -n, displays a detailed BLOCK PLAN
(highlighting any safety warnings) and asks for confirmation before running,
executes it from the current Git repository root (or current directory), and
streams stdout+stderr to both the terminal and {base_dir}/<session>/<step>.txt.

Refuses to overwrite an already-used step or skip a sequential step number.
At the end of execution, press Enter to copy the output to your clipboard or Esc to skip.

Configuration file ({config_path}):
  base_dir = /tmp/{prog}             Session and log directory
  work_dir = auto                    Working directory: auto (Git root or $PWD), cwd, or path
  agents_file = AGENTS.md            Default target file for --agents-install
  clipboard = prompt                 After execution: prompt | auto | never
  token_stats = true                 Show size & Claude/GPT/Gemini token counts: true | false
  shell = bash                       Shell executable used for syntax check and execution

Environment variables (override config file):
  RUN_BLOCK_CONFIG         Path to config file (default: {config_path})
  RUN_BLOCK_DIR            Override base_dir (default: {base_dir})
  RUN_BLOCK_CWD            Override work_dir for executed blocks
  RUN_BLOCK_AGENTS_FILE    Override default file for --agents-install (default: AGENTS.md)
  RUN_BLOCK_CLIPBOARD      Override clipboard mode: prompt | auto | never
  RUN_BLOCK_NO_CLIPBOARD=1 Alias for RUN_BLOCK_CLIPBOARD=never
  RUN_BLOCK_TOKEN_STATS    Override token_stats: 1/true or 0/false
  RUN_BLOCK_SHELL          Override shell executable (default: bash)
  RUN_BLOCK_UPDATE_URL     Override raw script URL for --update / --check-update
"""
